    "title": "The New Build",
    "tagline": "Design the department before it is built.",
    "seed": 1,
    "briefing": [
      "The hospital is building a new emergency department on the old car park. The walls go up in six months, and the board wants the floor plan from you.",
      "The shape is fixed: an L, with the public entrance on the west side and the ambulance bay at the south-east corner. So is the staffing. Everything inside is yours: where the waiting room, triage, the staff station, the bays and the trauma room go.",
      "The architect's first draft is loaded. It looks tidy on paper. Run a day in it before you sign anything: every metre a doctor walks is a minute a patient waits."
    ],
    "debrief": {
      "pass": [
        "The board signs off on your plan. Staff walk short loops from the station, and the ambulance crew wheels trauma patients straight into the resuscitation room.",
        "A good plan is invisible on the day. Nobody notices the corridor they did not have to walk."
      ],
      "fail": [
        "On paper the plan fitted. On the day, doctors spent their shift in the corridors, and every trip between the station and the bays came out of someone's wait.",
        "Look at the walking map: the brightest corridors are the ones to shorten. Put the station in the middle of the beds, triage beside the waiting room, and the trauma room by the ambulance door."
